## Engineering update · 5 October 2026

The [course desk update](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows) now marks #4471 closed:

- **Parser — fixed:** `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
  [GitHub issue #1](https://github.com/gniadzikm/mega-s01e03/issues/1) is closed as
  **completed** on the strength of that update, not an independently verified deployment.
- **Hint — won't fix:** **booking-v3 form retired**.
  [GitHub issue #2](https://github.com/gniadzikm/mega-s01e03/issues/2) is closed as
  **not planned**, not completed. Retirement is not a delivered hint fix.

These are the desk's reported outcomes, received after the initial submission. The
historical counts below still describe the export and are not rewritten by closure.
The five anomalous narratives remain unresolved evidence; the update does not explain them.

This review uses the **4 October export**, not the live support queue. The desk keeps working;
do not treat these counts as a current queue total. Run the components again with a fresh export
before merging or closing new reports.

## What the page actually shows

The next table preserves the export's original ticket assignments. Its “no ticket of its own”
label describes that export, not the separate GitHub issues linked later on this page.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table runs `uniqueById`, then `groupByCause` with the tenant directory from `locales.ts`.
`meta.browserLocale` and `meta.intakeTag` describe intake's guess, not the tenant's date order.
Do not count raw JSON rows, count tag names, or classify from the subject line.

- **Parser:** the shared parser reads month first for day-first tenants. For example,
  Harbour Dental's app report `R-41200` describes 7 April becoming 4 July.
- **Hint:** a day-first tenant using the **booking-v3 form** sees `MM/DD/YYYY`, while the form
  reads the tenant's day-first order. Copper Studio's form report `R-41230` belongs here despite
  its `parser` intake tag. App/email reports from the same tenant still route to parser.
- `dayFirst()` asks `Intl.DateTimeFormat(...).formatToParts(...)` for date-part order.
  Unknown tenants stay unplaced; never force them into the largest group.

<ReviewEvidence />

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## A better merge rule

**Match the underlying cause, not the words of the subject.** Read the body, tenant locale,
form version and channel. Matching subjects can hide different causes; different subjects can
describe the same cause. The running explorer below demonstrates both directions.

<DedupeExplorer />

When the evidence does not establish a cause, keep the report separate for investigation.
The old triage page and decision 0001 were last reviewed in 2024. Their apparent authority
does not overrule the live components; the layout marks pages older than its threshold as stale.
The recent review date on the old incident summary did not make its “one fix” conclusion true.

See the <a href="{base}/kb/triage/dedupe/">updated triage instructions</a>.
Decision 0001 is preserved as history,
not silently rewritten.

